WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
[Introductory studio tone] Welcome to Build 3D Websites with Kimi Code, Tutorial 4.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Take a screenshot or screen recording of a site you like, drop it into the chat, and study the layout and interaction.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Today, we'll use a ceramics website as an example to demonstrate layout, lighting, and interactive UI polish.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:25.000
With visual understanding, those design ideas are translated into clean code—taking the site to the next level.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:55.000
[Soft UI transition] Here is the second version: as the lighting shifts, the ceramic glaze starts to feel more and more real.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:30.000
As you scroll, the camera moves smoothly from side to side, paired with fine UI lines so the whole page feels dynamic and polished.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:03:05.000
To take things even further, you can connect third-party tools like Blender MCP for detailed 3D modeling or Unity MCP for 3D games.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:26.000
[Closing chime] Tell us what you'd like to build next, and explore the Accessible Career Gateway below!
